{title: Sublime gracia del Señor}
{artist: John Newton}
{key: F}

{comment: Verso 1}
[F]Sublime [F7]gracia [Bb]del [F]Señor
[F]Que a mí me [C7]transformó;
[F]Perdido [F7]estaba, [Bb]mas [F]Jesús
[Dm]Me halló [C7]y me [F]salvó.

{comment: Verso 2}
[F]Su gracia [F7]tierna [Bb]me [F]enseñó
[F]A amarle con [C7]temor,
[F]Y es su [F7]gracia [Bb]que [F]me da
[Dm]Certeza [C7]de su [F]amor.

{comment: Verso 3}
[F]Por pruebas [F7]y por [Bb]aflic[F]ción
[F]Yo he [C7]pasado ya;
[F]Su gracia [F7]nunca [Bb]me [F]faltó
[Dm]Y [C7]nunca [F]faltará.

{comment: Verso 4}
[F]Y cuando [F7]acabe [Bb]de [F]vivir
[F]Mi vida [C7]terrenal,
[F]Con Él, [F7]por gracia, [Bb]vivi[F]ré
[Dm]En gloria [C7]celes[F]tial.
